{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class P851C {\n    private static final double EPSILON = 1e-9;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        if (n > 11) {\n            System.out.println(0);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        int[][] pts = new int[n][5];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < 5; j++) {\n                pts[i][j] = sc.nextInt();\n            }\n        }\n\n        List<Integer> res = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            boolean flag = true;\n            for (int j = 0; j < n && flag; j++) {\n                if (j == i) continue;\n                for (int k = j + 1; k < n && flag; k++) {\n                    if (k == i) continue;\n                    Vector a = new Vector(pts[i], pts[j]);\n                    Vector b = new Vector(pts[i], pts[k]);\n                    double cosVal = a.inner(b) / (a.len() * b.len());\n                    if (Math.acos(cosVal) < Math.PI / 2 - EPSILON) {\n                        flag = false;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            if (flag) res.add(i + 1);\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(res.size());\n        for (int x : res) {\n            System.out.println(x);\n        }\n    }\n\n    static class Vector {\n        private final int[] coords;\n\n        Vector(int[] p, int[] q) {\n            coords = new int[5];\n            for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\n                coords[i] = q[i] - p[i];\n            }\n        }\n\n        double len() {\n            double s = 0;\n            for (int c : coords) s += (long) c * c;\n            return Math.sqrt(s);\n        }\n\n        int inner(Vector v) {\n            int sum = 0;\n            for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\n                sum += coords[i] * v.coords[i];\n            }\n            return sum;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport math\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    index = 1\n    \n    if n > 11:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    pts = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        point = []\n        for j in range(5):\n            point.append(int(data[index]))\n            index += 1\n        pts.append(point)\n    \n    res = []\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        flag = True\n        for j in range(n):\n            if not flag:\n                break\n            if j == i:\n                continue\n            for k in range(j + 1, n):\n                if not flag:\n                    break\n                if k == i:\n                    continue\n                \n                # Create vector a from point i to j\n                a_coords = [pts[j][p] - pts[i][p] for p in range(5)]\n                # Create vector b from point i to k\n                b_coords = [pts[k][p] - pts[i][p] for p in range(5)]\n                \n                # Calculate dot product\n                dot_product = sum(a_coords[p] * b_coords[p] for p in range(5))\n                \n                # Calculate lengths\n                a_len = math.sqrt(sum(c * c for c in a_coords))\n                b_len = math.sqrt(sum(c * c for c in b_coords))\n                \n                # Avoid division by zero\n                if a_len == 0 or b_len == 0:\n                    continue\n                \n                cos_val = dot_product / (a_len * b_len)\n                \n                # Clamp cos_val to [-1, 1] to avoid numerical issues\n                cos_val = max(-1, min(1, cos_val))\n                \n                angle = math.acos(cos_val)\n                \n                if angle < math.pi / 2 - 1e-9:\n                    flag = False\n                    break\n        \n        if flag:\n            res.append(i + 1)\n    \n    print(len(res))\n    for x in res:\n        print(x)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.4596363042946905e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.6464111215318553e-05, -0.22307373583316803, -0.25195738673210144, -0.06197478622198105, -0.00012361239350866526, -0.00022492263815365732, -0.45701864361763, -0.0008417400531470776, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -0.12730827927589417, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -0.0029459670186042786, -7.510157047363464e-06, -1.680836794548668e-05, -4.6491513785440475e-06, -0.00023648326168768108, -1.549708758830093e-05, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -0.06427612900733948, -4.7801782784517854e-05, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.3947389561508317e-05, -0.0077259535901248455, -4.529942543740617e-06, -0.43086645007133484, -5.960462772236497e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -8.582700684200972e-05, 0.0, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -